{
  "name": "cicada",
  "_about": "A cicada -- the great cicada (Lyristes plebejus), 3.5 cm long with wings of 4.5 cm: a stout broad-headed bug, the head as wide as the thorax, the eyes bulging at its corners, three ocelli on the crown, tiny bristle antennae, the ridged swollen face and a sucking beak beneath; a broad thorax, black marked ochre-orange; a short tapering abdomen ringed brown; and the great clear wings, longer than the body, held in a shallow roof over it, smoky-glassy, their strong veins green. Coat: the manna cicada (Cicada orni, grey-brown, the wings dotted). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/others.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, antennae that wave; the wings at rest as the animal holds them, beating in the variant \"flying\").",
